twisted.mail.smtp.SMTPClient and twisted.mail.pop3.POP3 now dot-stuff a line consisting of a single "." when the preceding CRLF and the "." fall on either side of a C{basic.FileSender} chunk boundary.  Previously the two could leave an unescaped C{\r\n.\r\n} inside the body, which a server could treat as the end of the C{DATA} payload and interpret the remainder as new SMTP commands (SMTP smuggling), or a C{RETR}/C{TOP} client could treat as the end of the message and truncate it.
